{"id":"0689f579-937f-48d4-bcdf-5d7453379df9","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter, supplied by the JVM to main, is never null in standard usage.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886489Z"}
{"id":"e8407bd3-adba-4a49-9af5-6fb39e9af9ec","expr":"args != null","rationale":"The 'args' parameter should be non-null during execution of 'main' as per Java runtime guarantees.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886934Z"}
{"id":"3288c6ea-e05d-4279-ba43-b746f895b4a1","expr":"b == 0 || a / b * b + a % b == a","rationale":"If b == 0, division is not performed; otherwise, basic property of integer division and modulus ensures this holds.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886574Z"}
{"id":"3796c23d-3035-47cc-8b9e-e20d9ba589f2","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"The length of an array in Java is always non-negative.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886934Z"}
{"id":"b0baef3b-0ac8-4938-88bf-c4407d1a04cb","expr":"args.length >= 0","rationale":"All arrays in Java have a non-negative length.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886489Z"}
{"id":"f7a1d858-7360-4827-9fdc-26642f51a035","expr":"b == 0 ? result == Integer.MIN_VALUE : result == a / b","rationale":"Captures the method's documented behavior: if b is 0, returns MIN_VALUE, else returns integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.887484Z"}
{"id":"1cd95f98-f40d-4cb6-ad64-d77dd5666c4b","expr":"args.getClass().isArray()","rationale":"The 'args' variable is always a Java array.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#main(String[]):void","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886489Z"}
{"id":"4f5ac5c2-d74e-4522-b7b7-5c99007d28ea","expr":"b != 0 || Integer.MIN_VALUE == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is 0, the method returns Integer.MIN_VALUE, so this invariant is trivially always true but conveys method's documented behavior.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886574Z"}
{"id":"7583256b-d46c-4faf-a996-be2d7b4344ed","expr":"b == 0 || result == a / b","rationale":"If b is not zero, result is exactly a / b.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.887484Z"}
{"id":"c6df33a7-165d-49bf-b167-ace37331128b","expr":"(b > 0) || (b <= 0)","rationale":"This covers all integer possibilities for b, and is useful as a partitioning fact.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886574Z"}
{"id":"9cd0d407-0c2d-4b06-972a-613c21f1278e","expr":"b == 0 || b * result <= a && a < b * (result + 1)","rationale":"If b != 0, result is integer division so this gives the mathematical bounds for a in integer division.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.887484Z"}
{"id":"263b4fdb-3252-4c9a-871d-6b472db10e15","expr":"a == 0 || a != 0","rationale":"This partitions the input space regarding 'a'; while tautological, it helps coverage analysis.","kind":"METHOD_ENTRY","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.886574Z"}
{"id":"2f73272c-9a79-46f5-9148-1f5c69b0054e","expr":"b != 0 || result == Integer.MIN_VALUE","rationale":"If b is zero, result must be Integer.MIN_VALUE.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.887484Z"}
{"id":"3f642e4c-e960-46f6-a0a4-2e12a08fbe6d","expr":"b == 0 || Math.abs(result) <= Math.abs(a)","rationale":"If b != 0, division reduces the magnitude or keeps it the same.","kind":"METHOD_EXIT","element":"com.example.Calc#safeDivide(int,int):int","file":"com/example/Calc.java","createdAt":"2026-04-19T04:34:42.887484Z"}
